      "sequence_id": 1,
      "text": "            The verb 'ser' is irregular and used to describe identity, origin or inherent qualities. \nIts forms include soy, eres, es, somos and son. \nThese drills practise changing sentences from singular to plural and vice versa while maintaining agreement in gender and number. \nFor example, 'Soy americano.' becomes 'Somos americanos.' when referring to multiple people. \nSimilarly, 'Es casada.' becomes 'Son casadas.' to agree with a plural feminine subject.\n"
